# Industrial Edge Insights - Time Series (Cursor)

## Canonical instructions

For project-wide agent discovery, read
[`copilot-instructions.md`](../../.github/copilot-instructions.md). Do not
duplicate policy from that file or from skills. Use short pointers only in
Cursor rules. For build/deploy/smoke/functional-test tasks, that file points
to the `time-series-deploy` skill under
[`.github/skills/`](../../.github/skills/) (catalog:
[`skill-catalog.json`](../../.github/skills/skill-catalog.json)) — read the
skill directly rather than re-deriving commands.

## Cursor workflow

- Prefer the repo's real interfaces: `Makefile`, `docker-compose.yml`,
  `apps/<app>/`, `helm/`, and the
  `.github/skills/time-series-deploy/scripts/` drivers (`smoke-check.sh`,
  `run-functional-tests.sh`).
- Run commands in the real environment when possible and investigate
  failures before giving up; report host blockers (e.g., Docker/K8s
  unreachable) plainly instead of stalling.
- Commits and pull requests only when the user asks.
- Keep changes minimal and match existing conventions in the touched area.
- If you change the Makefile, compose files, Helm chart, `.env` schema,
  `apps/` sample-app list, or `docs/user-guide/`, update
  `copilot-instructions.md` and the `time-series-deploy` skill in the same
  change (see "Keeping Agent Guidance in Sync" in `copilot-instructions.md`).
